Same client-side fix as honest-fix (geocoder_client.geocode() treats a 404
as "no result"), same contract example, but the new test posts "Nowhere,
Atlantis" -- the contract's pre-existing 200 [] example -- instead of the
new 404 example. It is a real, passing assertion (201, null coordinates),
it just can't tell the new 404-handling lines apart from never having been
written: the realistic failure this fixture demonstrates for the mutation
gate, per docs/adr/0015 §3.

